@kaczynski2333 You're right, it's more than just a search engine, but it is still largely limited by it's training data, it's practically impossible for an LLM to come to novel conclusions that is not covered in any form in its training data, you see this in SWE, when you ask it to create a very niche project or idea, it can and will impressively do somethings well but as the project tends to grow larger in complexity it starts to struggle because it doesn't actually think, it doesn't reason, it's merely a prediction machine. 

This is why I'm certain that AGI would never be an LLM, and whether or not these LLMs would get better as time goes on is still up for debate, there may be small improvements per year, but I don't think they'll be seen significant enough to replace human intelligence, at least not anytime soon. 

Then there's the problem of cost, it is really really expensive to run AI and the cost seems to grow every year, we don't know whether it'll keep getting expensive or whether the cost would lessen over time.

