@brrfibgtun LLM chatbots are merely statistical language models, useful for language tasks.  In AI Psychosis, yes, the chatbot is a mirror, in most other areas LLMs are merely a tool, and a blinking cursor on a command-line interface was never a great UI strategy for user exploration of features.

LLM chatbot deployment and user adoption has been a complete mess, so fair call that many see it as the latest vapourware.

Look to Claude Code and Palantir's Maven to understand how user adoption should have gone.  There will be similar progress in some other sectors, but it's not the magical tech we've all been sold.

