@MarkSavant I'm bullish on medicine.  Sure, you can sign up to telemedicine or a future online AI platform, but most people will want to deal with humans with people skills (note:  it has been my experience that many doctors and surgeons have zero people skills).  Also, jobs that require professional certifications or schooling with limited enrollments and high barriers to entry are good.  Many such jobs exist in healthcare.

So, a little about me.  I retired in my early 40s.  Life happens;  I lost enough money that I had to re-enter the workforce.  My previous career is not nearly as lucrative as it once was, so I decided to get into software development.  This was right at the apex in like 2022.  I did a short stint at AWS and decided quickly that Big Tech was not for me.  Nor do I feel like it is a good career right now with AI.  

So I was a caregiver to a relative with a terminal condition during part of the first retirement.  I have a natural rapport with old people.  I have decided to get into nursing, am taking pre-reqs right now, and plan to attend RN school in the spring.  Ultimately, I plan to go to grad school and become a CRNA.  I suppose that I will be the oldest, but whatever.  I have a baby face and most people think that I am early 30s, so I guess that is good.  Cheers.

